=== Nullable(String): barewords NaN, NULLIFY and NULL parse as strings (JSONEachRow legacy string-wrapped) ===
1	['NaN','a']
2	['NULL','b']
3	['NULLIFY','c']
4	['d','nan']
=== Nullable(String): barewords in VALUES string-wrapped and CSV ===
1	['NaN','a']
2	['NULL','b']
5	['NaN','e']
6	['NULL','f']
=== Nullable(Enum8): bareword starting with N parses via CSV (released form) ===
1	['no','yes']
=== Nullable(Float64): NaN and native NULL still parse (N/n -> quoted dispatch kept for non-string types) ===
1	[nan,1.5,2]
2	[3.5]
3	[4.5]
=== Nullable(UInt64): native NULL parses, quoted number kept ===
1	[1,2]
